    summary: `# 🧬 Rec Adv Bioscience #3.2 — Recent Advance in Bacteriology

## 🎯 Modern bacterial diagnostic landscape
- Beyond classic culture + Gram stain + biochemistry
- Molecular tools (PCR, MALDI-TOF, WGS) revolutionizing
- Faster (minutes-hours vs days)
- More specific (strain typing, virulence, AMR)

## 🔬 Bacterial identification methods

### Classical
- Gram stain (G+ vs G-, cocci vs rod)
- Culture on selective + differential media
- Biochemical tests (oxidase, catalase, coagulase, sugar fermentation)
- API kits (commercial multi-test strips)
- Vitek 2 (automated biochem)

### MALDI-TOF MS
- Rapid bacterial ID (minutes)
- Spectral fingerprint matching to library
- Standard in modern clinical labs
- Limitations: requires library, similar species can confuse

### 16S rRNA sequencing
- Universal bacterial gene
- Sanger sequence ~700-1500 bp
- Match BLAST database
- Genus-level usually, sometimes species
- Useful for unculturable bacteria

### Whole genome sequencing (WGS)
- NGS technology (Illumina, Oxford Nanopore)
- Complete genome → strain typing, AMR, virulence
- Outbreak investigation (SNP analysis)
- Becoming standard in surveillance
- TH NIAH + universities have capacity

## 🦠 Antimicrobial Resistance (AMR) detection

### Phenotypic
- Disk diffusion (Kirby-Bauer)
- MIC (broth microdilution, E-test)
- Etest gradient strip

### Genotypic
- PCR for resistance genes (mecA, blaCTX-M, blaNDM, etc.)
- WGS for full resistome
- ESBL, MRSA, VRE, CRE detection

### MIC concept
- Minimum Inhibitory Concentration
- CLSI breakpoints (S/I/R)
- PK/PD considerations
- Detail in lecture 7

## 🦠 Virulence factor + typing

### Specific PCR for virulence genes
- ETEC fimbriae (F4, F5, F6, F18)
- STEC stx genes
- *S. suis* mrp, epf, sly
- Pasteurella PMT toxin

### Strain typing methods
- PFGE (pulsed-field gel electrophoresis) — historical
- MLST (multilocus sequence typing) — 7 housekeeping genes
- WGS-based (cgMLST, wgMLST) — modern standard
- Spa typing (S. aureus)
- Capsular typing (S. suis, K. pneumoniae)

## 🦠 Bacterial-specific diagnostics in vet

### Brucella
- Rose Bengal, CFT, ELISA, FPA
- Culture (BSL-3)
- PCR (Bcsp31, IS711)

### Mycobacterium bovis
- Tuberculin test (DTH)
- IFN-γ release assay (BoviGAM)
- PCR (IS6110, MPB70)
- Mycobacterial growth indicator tube (MGIT)

### Mycoplasma
- PCR (most sensitive — culture difficult)
- ELISA serology
- Specific media (PPLO broth)

### Anaerobes
- Special transport (anaerobic medium)
- Culture in anaerobic chamber
- Slow growing
- Often syndrome-based dx

### Rickettsia (covered in 5.2)
- IFA, PCR (no culture in BSL-3)

## 🇹🇭 Thailand bacteriology infrastructure
- **NIAH** — DLD reference
- **CU vet, KU vet, ChM vet, KKU vet** — university labs
- **CDC — TH** — public health
- **MALDI-TOF** in major centers
- **WGS** capacity at NSTDA, BIOTEC, Mahidol, CU, KU

## 📝 EXAM RECAP
1. ⭐ MALDI-TOF MS = standard bacterial ID (minutes)
2. ⭐ 16S rRNA = universal, genus-level usually
3. ⭐ WGS = strain typing, AMR, virulence (modern standard)
4. ⭐ MIC = key AMR phenotypic measure
5. ⭐ Genotypic AMR: mecA, blaCTX-M, blaNDM, etc.`,
