    summary: `# 🧬 Rec Adv Bioscience #4.2 — Clinical Vet Immunology

## 🎯 Immune system overview
- Innate (rapid, non-specific) — physical barrier, phagocytes, complement
- Adaptive (specific, memory) — B + T cells

## 🔬 Innate immunity

### Physical/chemical
- Skin, mucus, lysozyme, low pH
- Antimicrobial peptides (defensins, cathelicidins)

### Cells
- Neutrophil — first responder, phagocytic
- Macrophage — phagocytic + antigen presenting
- NK cell — kill virus-infected, tumor
- Mast cell, eosinophil — parasite + allergy
- Basophil — allergy

### Soluble factors
- Complement (classical, alternative, lectin pathways)
- Cytokines (IFN, TNF, IL-1, IL-6, IL-8)
- Acute-phase proteins (CRP, SAA, haptoglobin) — vet biomarkers!

### Pattern recognition
- TLR (Toll-like receptors)
- NLR (NOD-like receptors)
- RLR (RIG-I-like)
- Recognize PAMPs (Pathogen-Associated Molecular Patterns)

## 🔬 Adaptive immunity

### B cells (humoral)
- Bone marrow origin
- Antibody (Ig) production
- 5 classes: IgM, IgG, IgA, IgE, IgD
  - IgM: first, pentamer, complement
  - IgG: most abundant, neonate via colostrum
  - IgA: mucosal, dimer, secretory
  - IgE: allergy, parasite
  - IgD: B cell receptor

### T cells (cellular)
- Thymus origin
- CD4+ helper (Th1, Th2, Th17, Treg)
  - Th1 → cell-mediated (IFN-γ)
  - Th2 → humoral, allergy (IL-4, IL-5)
  - Th17 → inflammation (IL-17)
  - Treg → tolerance (IL-10, TGF-β)
- CD8+ cytotoxic — kill virus-infected, tumor
- γδ T cells — esp. ruminant, mucosal

## 🐾 Immune assays in vet

### Antibody quantification
- **ELISA** — quantitative, common
- **IFA** — fluorescent slide, semi-quant
- **Western blot** — confirmatory
- **Virus neutralization (VN)** — functional
- **HAI** — flu, NDV serotyping

### Cellular function
- **CBC + differential** — basic
- **Flow cytometry** — phenotype (CD4, CD8, B cells)
- **Lymphocyte proliferation** — research
- **IFN-γ release assay (BoviGAM)** — bovine TB
- **Cytokine ELISA** — inflammation

### Allergy testing
- **Intradermal test** — gold standard
- **Serum IgE ELISA** — convenient
- **Basophil activation** — research

## 🐾 Key clinical immunological diseases

### Immunodeficiency
- **FeLV** — feline retrovirus, lymphoma + immunosuppression
- **FIV** — feline AIDS analogue
- **Bovine BLV** — leukosis
- **Equine SCID** — Arabian foals
- **Canine X-linked SCID** — dogs

### Hypersensitivity (4 types)
- I: IgE-mediated allergy (atopy, anaphylaxis)
- II: cytotoxic Ab (IMHA, ITP)
- III: immune complex (PDNS, glomerulonephritis)
- IV: T cell-mediated (delayed — TB skin test, contact dermatitis)

### Autoimmune
- IMHA (immune-mediated hemolytic anemia) — Coombs+
- ITP (immune-mediated thrombocytopenia)
- Pemphigus (skin)
- SLE
- Polymyositis

### Vaccine immunology
- Live vs killed
- Adjuvant
- Mucosal vaccines (intranasal, oral)
- Maternal antibody interference (timing of vax)
- DIVA strategy (gE-deleted PR vaccine, etc.)

## 📝 EXAM RECAP
1. ⭐ Innate (rapid, non-specific) + Adaptive (specific, memory)
2. ⭐ Acute-phase proteins (CRP, SAA, haptoglobin) = vet biomarkers
3. ⭐ Hypersensitivity 4 types: I IgE, II cytotoxic, III IC, IV T cell
4. ⭐ Flow cytometry = phenotype lymphocytes (CD4, CD8)
5. ⭐ FeLV/FIV/BLV/SCID = vet immunodeficiency`,
